LOCAL GOVERNMENT ACT 1976

LOCAL GOVERNMENT (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES)

(FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2025

IN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 102(t) of the Local Government

Act 1976 [Act 171], as extended and modified by the Federal Territory of Labuan

(Extension and Modification of Local Government Act 1976) Order 2010

[P.U. (A) 439/2010]), the Perbadanan Labuan makes, and pursuant to section 103

of the Act, the Minister confirms, the following by-laws:

Citation and commencement

1. (1) These by-laws may be cited as the Local Government (Compounding

of Offences) (Federal Territory of Labuan) By-Laws 2025.

(2) These By-Laws come into operation on 2 May 2025.

Compoundable offences

2. (1) The offences specified in the First Schedule are prescribed to be

compoundable offences.

(2) The compoundable offences may be compounded with the consent in writing

of the Public Prosecutor in Form 1 of the Second Schedule.

Procedure for compounding

3. (1) Upon receipt of any information or complaint that a compoundable offence

has been committed, the Chief Executive Officer or any officer authorized in writing

by the Perbadanan Labuan may, with the consent in writing of the Public Prosecutor

referred to in paragraph 2(2), issue an offer to compound the offence in Form 2

of the Second Schedule.

(2) An offer to compound an offence shall be valid for a period of fourteen days

starting from the date the offer is received by the person to whom offer is made or such

extended period as the Chief Executive Officer or any officer authorized in writing

by the Perbadanan Labuan may grant, and if full payment of the sum offered is made on

or before the expiry of the period of fourteen days or such extended period granted,

no further proceedings shall be taken against the person who committed such offence.

Acceptance of compound

4. A person who accepts an offer to compound a compoundable offence

shall accept the offer in Form 3 of the Second Schedule and return the Form 3 to the

Chief Executive Officer or any officer authorized in writing by the Perbadanan Labuan.

Payment of compound

5. (1) If an offer to compound an offence is accepted by the person to whom

the offer is made, the person shall pay the compound—

(a) in cash and shall be delivered personally to the Chief Executive Officer

or any officer authorized in writing by the Perbadanan Labuan to the

address specified in Form 2 of the Second Schedule;

(b) by money order, postal order, cashier's cheque or bank draft

crossed with the words "Account Payee Only" made payable

to the Perbadanan Labuan and shall be delivered personally or sent

by registered post to the Chief Executive Officer or any officer

authorized in writing by the Perbadanan Labuan to the address

specified in Form 2 of the Second Schedule; or

(c) through credit card, debit card, charge card or any other forms

of electronic fund transfer into the Perbadanan Labuan's account.

(2) The Chief Executive Officer or any officer authorized in writing

by the Perbadanan Labuan shall issue an official receipt for every payment received

under paragraph (1) to the person to whom the offer to compound an offence is made.

(3) An official receipt issued under paragraph (2) shall include any electronic

receipt if the payment is made through an electronic fund transfer.

Sum of money to be collected

6. The sum of money to be collected by the Perbadanan Labuan for

compounding an offence under the Act or an offence specified in the First Schedule

shall not exceed the maximum amount of fine as provided in the Act for the offence.

Prosecution may be instituted if no payment made

7. If no payment of the compound offered is made within the period

specified in paragraph 3(2), prosecution may be instituted without further notice.

